11
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:40,160
His mother Claire worked for a modeling agency.

12
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:43,800
His father Richard imported vintage cars from America.

13
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:49,200
He grew up with two older sisters, Elizabeth and Victoria, and the family was comfortable

14
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:51,280
but not famous, not even close.

15
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:55,160
If you had asked anyone on his street what little rob would become, nobody would have

16
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:56,520
said movie star.

17
00:00:56,520 --> 00:01:01,880
He went to the Herodian school, a private school in London, and he was the kind of kid who

18
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:04,880
was more interested in music than in lessons.

19
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:09,200
He taught him so piano and guitar, and he wrote songs in his bedroom long before he ever

20
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:10,360
read a script.

21
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:15,160
When he was about 12, his sisters modeling work opened a door, and he did a little modeling

22
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:16,360
himself.

23
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:20,440
It did not last, and the work dried up by the time he was 15.

24
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:23,720
So at 15 he did something small that changed everything.

25
00:01:23,720 --> 00:01:28,760
He joined a local amateur group called the Barnes Theatre Company, starting out backstage

26
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:30,680
before taking small parts.

27
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:32,720
He was not a star in that room.

28
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:37,080
He was the kid who showed up, but when he played in their production of Tess of the Derbe

29
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:39,600
Wills, a talent agent saw him.

30
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,600
And that was the first real door.

31
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:44,040
His first screen jobs were tiny.

32
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:49,000
In 2004 he had a part in a German television fantasy called Ring of the Nebelongs, which

33
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,960
in some countries was released as Sword of Zantin.

34
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:54,240
Ring came a much more painful early lesson.

35
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:59,400
He filmed scenes for the film Vanity Fair, with Reese Witherspoon, and almost all of his

36
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:01,800
scenes were cut from the final film.

37
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:05,080
He had worked on a real movie, and the audience barely saw him.

38
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:09,360
For a long time he was an actor who auditioned a lot and booked very little.

39
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:13,400
Then in 2005 came Harry Potter and The Goblet of Fire.

40
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:18,800
He was cast as Cedric Degree, the handsome decent Hufflepuff champion who's chosen alongside

41
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,240
Harry for the tri-visit tournament.

42
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:24,600
Cedric was a perfect part for a young actor nobody had heard of.

43
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:29,080
He is likable, good at everything, and then at the end of the film he dies.

44
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:31,080
Millions of people saw that scene.

45
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:33,760
The internet called him the handsome Hufflepuff.

46
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:38,000
For the first time, strangers knew his face, and none of them knew his name.

47
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,160
His next step was almost a dead end, and he has joked about that too.

48
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:47,240
In the years after Harry Potter he went to audition after audition, and kept losing parts.

49
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:51,280
In 2007 and 2008 he was playing small roles.

50
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:56,280
He kept playing music at open mic nights in London in small spars and pubs, and he kept

51
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:57,680
going to castings.

52
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:03,000
In 2008 he walked into an audition for a film based on a young adult vampire novel called

53
