79
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:32,080
Critics were surprised, the teen idol could act, and he could be strange.

80
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:37,080
He appeared in water for elephants, in remember me, in Bellamy, and in each of them he was

81
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:39,320
trying out a different version of himself.

82
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:42,320
Not every film worked, some were quickly forgotten.

83
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:47,800
And he kept taking jobs where the pay was low, and the director was someone he admired.

84
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:49,000
That was the plan.

85
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:53,560
He has described it as using the money and fame from Twilight to buy himself a different

86
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:54,960
career.

87
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:57,840
That is why the next few years look so odd on paper.

88
00:04:57,840 --> 00:05:03,080
In 2014, he starred in the Rover, a dusty, violent Australian thriller from director David

89
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:06,960
Mischot, where he played a slow, damaged young man named Ray.

90
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:10,880
In the same year, he was in maps to the stars with Cronenberg again.

91
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:16,200
In 2016, he was part of the cast of the Lost City of Z, a jungle adventure film from director

92
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:17,440
James Gray.

93
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:21,040
These were films that his old fans did not go to sea.

94
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:25,360
Critics did, though, and a smaller audience began to notice that the vampire could do things

95
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:26,840
the vampire could not.

96
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:31,840
The turning point came in 2017 with a film called Good Time, directed by Josh and Benny

97
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:32,840
Safty.

98
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:37,680
He plays a small time criminal named Connie, who tries to rescue his brother after a bank

99
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:42,920
